# Before writing or changing music, read music/README.md (style, moods, format).
title    Peaks
composer Claude
about    Thin air above the clouds: an oboe in B Dorian, echoed an eighth later across the valley, over harp arpeggios with added seconds, a high string pad and a bell. In 6/8. When something is near, timpani, triangle and a bodhran take over; horns call for a fight, choir and gong for a guardian.
tempo    56
beats    2
steps    6
reverb   0.45

# moods (music/README.md)
# mood explore:  lead echo harp pad bass bell
# mood treasure: harp pad bell wonder
# mood sense:    timpani tri bodhran pad bass bell
# mood rise:     sense lead echo harp snare
# mood fight:    rise -echo -bell -harp -tri horn brass drive war crash
# mood boss:     fight -lead choir gong

voice lead     oboe      vol=0.6  pan=-0.15
voice echo     oboe      vol=0.22 pan=0.45 rev=0.6
voice horn     horn      vol=0.65  pan=0.2  oct=-1 att=0.025 rel=0.12 rev=0.3
voice harp     harp      vol=0.5  pan=0.25
voice pad      strings   vol=0.26 pan=-0.25 center=F#4 att=0.6 rel=1
voice bass     upright   vol=0.7
voice bell     bell      vol=0.2  pan=0.35 rev=0.7
voice wonder   celesta   vol=0.38 pan=-0.3 rev=0.6
voice timpani  timpani   vol=0.55 pan=-0.1
voice tri      tri       vol=0.3  pan=0.4
voice bodhran  bodhran   vol=0.55 pan=-0.2
voice snare    snare     vol=0.3  pan=0.1
voice brass    brass     vol=0.42 pan=-0.25 gate=0.65 center=F#4 att=0.018 rel=0.09 rev=0.22
voice crash    crash     vol=0.28 pan=0.2
voice choir    choir     vol=0.3  center=B3 att=0.5 rel=0.8
voice gong     gong      vol=0.3  pan=-0.3

# Combat-only motion: tight low ostinato and accented battle drums, at the same tempo.
voice drive    pizz      vol=0.52 pan=-0.35 gate=0.65 rev=0.3
voice war      tommid    vol=0.5  pan=0.15 rev=0.25

# Bm E Bm A | G A Bm Bm: the motif (B C# D F# E), the E major chord is the Dorian colour
pattern A
